# Cloud Cram Core Rules

## Project identity

- **Study Sessions (Cloud Cram)** — static HTML/JS PWA for certification practice quizzes (cloud, security, Linux).
- **Repo:** https://github.com/earthboundtrev/cloud_computing_quizzes
- Root **`README.MD`** is the product overview. Do not rewrite it casually. Put **new technical docs** in existing pattern guides or focused markdown at repo root only when the user asks.

## Architecture (mental model)

| Layer | Role |
|-------|------|
| `*_quiz.html` + `quiz-init-*.js` | Per-quiz shell; wires bank + config into `QuizEngine.run()` |
| `quiz-engine.js` | Shared engine: modes, scoring, import/export, weighted sampling, case-study UI |
| `data/*-questions.js` (+ objectives, case studies, scenarios) | Question banks and metadata |
| `quiz-config.js` | Quiz catalog, order, completion badges (`localStorage`) |
| `index.html` / `index-init.js` | Hub and navigation |
| `sw.js` / `sw-register.js` | Offline precache; bump `CACHE_NAME` when precache list changes |
| `brain-dump.js` | Per-question notes — **IndexedDB** (`StudySessionsBrainDumps`), localStorage fallback |
| `session-streak.js`, `motivation.js` | Engagement — **localStorage** |
| `rhcsa-migration.js` | One-time **localStorage** migrations (idempotent flags) |
| `app-reset.js` | Clears localStorage + IndexedDB |
| `scripts/*.js` | Node validators (banks, SW precache, CISSP, migrations) — no bundler |

Progress keys follow `study_sessions_profile_{quizId}` in localStorage. Changing keys or shapes requires migration scripts and regression tests.

## Product principles

- **Offline-first** — no backend; service worker precaches static assets.
- **Local-only progress** — quiz stats, order, brain dumps stay in the browser unless the user exports results.
- **Bank integrity** — new/changed questions must pass bank lint and stay wired in HTML + `sw.js` precache when applicable.

## Scope and quality

- **Minimal diffs** — match existing IIFE style, `var` in legacy modules, and naming in sibling quizzes.
- **Ticket workflow:** pointer pipeline `IMPLEMENT → BUGBOT → TESTS → ARCHITECT → DEPLOY` until human sign-off — `.cursor/rules/ticket-lifecycle-loop.mdc`. Any code fix rewinds to **BUGBOT**.

## Model strategy (ticket work)

Human approval happens at **issue/PR intent**. Use **different agents/models per role** (`.cursor/rules/ticket-lifecycle-loop.mdc`). **Cost default (aligned with Ducking Gravity / SmartAstro 8/18/2026):** implement on Composer Fast; Bugbot/Architect/security on **Grok 4.6 High** — do **not** omit `model` on checks (costly default) and do **not** burn Opus/Sonnet on routine reviews.

| Phase | Stage | Who / what | Primary → fallback(s) |
|-------|-------|------------|------------------------|
| **Implement** | IMPLEMENT | Parent / implement Task | `composer-2.5-fast` → `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` |
| **Bugbot** | BUGBOT | Separate **`bugbot`** Task — never self-review | `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast` → `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` → omit |
| **Tests** | TESTS | Same session | — |
| **Architect** | ARCHITECT | Separate Architect Task (`review-architect`) | `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast` → `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` → omit |
| **Deploy** | DEPLOY | Default Agent | Composer → Grok / parent |
| **Security** | (within BUGBOT→DEPLOY) | `security-review` when risky | `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast` → `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` → omit |

Outages: `.cursor/rules/subagent-watchdog.mdc`. Prefer local Tasks: `.cursor/rules/prefer-local-agents.mdc`.

**Architect blockers → rewind pointer to BUGBOT**, then forward through TESTS and ARCHITECT again.

Do **not** run the heavy architect review before implementation unless the user explicitly asks for upfront design on a large/cross-cutting change.

## Git workflow (GitHub)

**Before writing code** for a GitHub issue or feature branch, sync with `main`.

### 1. Load issue context

- Run `gh issue view {N}` for acceptance criteria.
- Note the issue number for commits and PR description (`Closes #N`).

### 2. Update local `main`

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main
git pull origin main
```

### 3. Branch

```bash
git checkout -b feature/short-description-{N}
```

Continuing branch: merge `origin/main` (not rebase unless the user asks). Resolve conflicts before new commits.

### 4. During implementation

- Work on the feature branch only — never commit directly to `main` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not open the PR until §5a and §5b are complete.
- **Never** commit secrets, API keys, or user quiz exports with PII.

### 5a. BUGBOT & TESTS stages

Pipeline: `.cursor/rules/ticket-lifecycle-loop.mdc`. Pointer reaches **TESTS** only after **BUGBOT** is clean on the current diff.

#### BUGBOT (repeat until clean)

- Launch **Bugbot** per Cursor `review-bugbot` skill (`Diff: branch changes`).
- Fix valid findings → stay at **BUGBOT**, re-run on updated diff.

#### TESTS (after Bugbot clean)

Run the same checks as CI (`.github/workflows/lint.yml`):

```bash
node scripts/lint-banks.js --ci
node scripts/check-sw-precache.js
node scripts/check-page-banks.js
node scripts/validate-cissp-questions.js
node scripts/smoke-test-cissp.js
node scripts/lint-cissp-questions.js
```

When touching related areas, also run targeted scripts:

- `node scripts/test-rhcsa-migration.js` — after `rhcsa-migration.js` or profile key changes
- `node scripts/test-cissp.js` — CISSP bank/engine changes (wraps validate/smoke/lint)

Failures or material test-driven code changes → rewind pointer to **BUGBOT**.

### 5b. ARCHITECT stage

**After BUGBOT clean and TESTS pass.** Blockers fixed → **rewind to BUGBOT**, then TESTS → ARCHITECT again.

Run **`review-architect`** or `.cursor/rules/cloud-cram-architect.mdc` as a **separate** Task with **`model: "cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast"`**.

For service worker, storage, import parsing, or new network use: also run **security-review** per `.cursor/rules/security-review.mdc`.

### 5c. DEPLOY stage

**Only after ARCHITECT merge-ready.**

1. Re-run CI commands above (full set when risky).
2. Push; open/update PR with **`Closes #N`** in the body.
3. Watch GitHub Actions — code changes → **IMPLEMENT**, then **BUGBOT** before skipping ahead.
4. Merge/close **only when the human explicitly asks**.
5. After merge: verify issue `#N` is **CLOSED**; delete the feature branch when asked.

### 6. Confirm before coding

```bash
git branch --show-current
git log --oneline -1 origin/main
git status -sb
```

## Deploy / cache hygiene

- Static hosting (e.g. Netlify): `_headers`, `_redirects` at repo root.
- After changing precached assets: update `PRECACHE_PATHS` in `sw.js` and bump `CACHE_NAME`.
- After JS/CSS logic changes: bump `?v=` query on script/link tags in affected HTML (see comment in `quiz-config.js`).

